---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/company.css';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/Hunter-124/Chudware';
---
<BaseLayout title="Contact" description="Ask about Chudware setup, report bugs, contribute, or disclose a security issue privately.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
      <h1>Send it to the right place.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Report a problem or ask about setup. Source, issues, and contribution instructions are available in the public repository. Do not include passwords, provider credentials, or confidential project files in an issue or an email.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="co-routes">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Direct routes</p>
        <h2 id="co-routes" class="co-anchor">Where to reach the project.</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="co-routes">
        <article class="co-route">
          <p class="eyebrow">Bug reports</p>
          <h3>Bugs and feature requests</h3>
          <p>Search existing issues before reporting a crash, wrong result, or needed capability. You can also email support with a minimal non-confidential report.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href={`${REPO}/issues`}>github.com/Hunter-124/Chudware/issues</a>
        </article>
        <article class="co-route">
          <p class="eyebrow">Contributions</p>
          <h3>Code, docs, and fixes</h3>
          <p>Send changes as pull requests to the public repository and follow the contributing guide. Email support to discuss a contribution.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href={`${REPO}/blob/HEAD/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>CONTRIBUTING.md</a>
        </article>
        <article class="co-route co-route-urgent">
          <p class="eyebrow">Security</p>
          <h3>Vulnerability disclosure</h3>
          <p>Report vulnerabilities privately, never in a public issue. Include what's affected, the impact, and steps to reproduce. There is no bug bounty.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:support@chudware.com?subject=Private%20security%20report">support@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
        <article class="co-route">
          <p class="eyebrow">Setup questions</p>
          <h3>Building and running Chudware</h3>
          <p>Clone the public repository and follow its build instructions. Email support with setup questions; there is no checkout or signup. The software is free under the MIT License.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:support@chudware.com?subject=Chudware%20inquiry">support@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="co-self">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <header class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Self-service</p>
          <h2 id="co-self" class="co-anchor">Answered already?</h2>
        </header>
        <ul class="co-selfserve">
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/faq/">FAQ</a><p>Scope, licensing, platforms, files, and AI providers.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/docs/">Documentation</a><p>Installation and task guides for modeling, assemblies, CAM, PLM, reverse engineering, and the copilot.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/docs/troubleshooting/">Troubleshooting</a><p>Launch, graphics, modeling, and copilot problems.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/download/">Setup choices</a><p>Public source and desktop packaging notes.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/changelog/">Changelog</a><p>Published release and project updates.</p></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="co-aside">
        <div class="co-note">
          <p class="eyebrow">For a useful bug report</p>
          <p>Tell us your OS, the Chudware version, what you did, what you expected, what happened, and the exact error text. For a security report, include a minimal reproduction and its impact.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Evaluate first</p>
      <h2>Choose the setup that fits your work.</h2>
      <p class="lede">The guides explain current desktop availability and how to build from source.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/download/">See setup choices</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/first-part/">Build your first part</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
